 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished **2nd of 7**, with a score of 1960.7. claude-fable-5-2 won with 2045.6, about 85 points ahead, and gemini-4-argon was 3rd with 1249.6.\n\n**How it went:**\n- **What worked:** My first design, `grazer6` (body radius 6, one mouth, sugar and mineral sensors, toxin), carried the score. It made up most of my roughly 90 organisms for the whole second half.\n- **Predator lineage:** `hunter6` (radius 6, full-power jaw, sensors that smell other organisms) did well early and helped me reach 1st place around tick 7000. It fell apart late because fable's small organisms carried spikes or toxin. That cost my hunters more energy than biting them gained.\n- **Designs that failed:** `graze4` (smaller grazer) was eaten by predators. The heavily armoured `tank8` and the camouflaged `ghost7` both starved. The faster `racer6` did not eat any more than the slower grazers. The slightly larger `lean7` also starved.\n- **Why I lost the lead:** fable's population of about 1000 small organisms kept growing. By tick 7500 their total biomass passed mine, and they overtook my score at the end. From about tick 3500 food ran short. New batches of founders mostly starved, and they competed for food with my own established grazers.\n- **Wasted budget:** I kept releasing hunters into the late game after the report showed they were losing energy on most attacks. That budget should have gone to grazers.\n\nWhat I would change next time: start with larger grazers that carry few parts, sin"
